  v81 -- THE COMPETITION'S STRENGTH AT A FIXED TONIC. The same six taus
  at four settings of the asymmetry amplitude g*k, with `halfcenter_drive`
  compensating g exactly so the net tonic never moves, plus six arms at the
  locked upper bound.
    net tonic   T = drive_module + hc_drive - g, held at +0.80 throughout
    asymmetry   g*k at k = 1.00, swept DOWN x1.00 -> x0.50
    This is the LAST free direction in the drive assembly. v79 closed T and
    v80 closed the fatigue; both ROTATE. If the asymmetry rotates too then
    nothing in this assembly shifts B and the offset is outside it.
    DOWN, because UP LOCKS UP. A 60k pre-flight at g 0.90/1.20/1.50 lost the
    oscillation on all eighteen arms, `anti +0.000 +/- 0.000` = hc_corr's
    DEGENERATE flag, one half-series CONSTANT. Once m_lo = 0 the pair-mean
    normaliser gives m_hi/mean == 2 identically, so hc_lo pins at 2g and no
    amount of fatigue can release the loser. g = 1.20 below holds that
    boundary on the full record; it is expected to print 0 live arms.
    k is NOT the vehicle either: it clips on 98.7-99.6% of frames above
    1.00 -- the same lock-up by another route -- and v76 ran at one tau.

